          "distinct": true,
          "id": "edaf6a0c41292f651d53954a61cabb7472348111",
          "message": "Automated Ruby Gem release pipeline and Cross Platform CI fixes  (#738)\n\n* feat: Implement Ruby port release pipeline with cross-platform testing\n\n* fix: Correct working directory for Ruby tests to fix path resolution\n\n* fix: Robust environment setup and library path resolution for Ruby tests\n\n* fix: Absolute path resolution and Windows DLL search path for Ruby tests\n\n* fix: Define global METACALL_INSTALL_PATH and dynamic library paths for all OSs\n\n* fix: Direct METACALL_INSTALL_PATH pointer to lib directory for all platforms\n\n* fix: Create symbolic library links to satisfy strict regex in Ruby wrapper\n\n* fix: Define internal MetaCall plugin paths and force library symlinks\n\n* fix: Universal MetaCall library detection for Ruby port tests\n\n* fix: Robust cross-platform library detection for Ruby port tests\n\n* fix: Implement forensic detection and direct library injection for Ruby tests\n\n* fix: Implement dynamic binary detection for robust cross-platform Ruby tests\n\n* fix: Implement fuzzy library matching and absolute path injection for Ruby tests\n\n* fix: Robust library detection using system trace and fuzzy matching\n\n* fix: Implement Guix Store Scraper for total MetaCall loader visibility\n\n* fix: Implement multi-house path discovery for Guix and macOS debug libraries\n\n* fix: Robust multi-path component detection and trailing colon fix for Ruby tests\n\n* fix: Implement universal Bash-based detection for Windows, Ubuntu, and macOS\n\n* fix: Robust cross-platform detection with conditional path checking and non-fatal pipes\n\n* fix: Robust multi-platform detection using pipe-safe Bash and conditional paths\n\n* fix: Final safe partition for Unix Bash and Windows PowerShell to resolve encoding and path issues\n\n* fix: Robust cross-platform environment detection with pipe-safe Bash and BOM-free PowerShell\n\n* fix: Final Windows PowerShell compatibility fix for environment writing\n\n* fix: Final Windows environment encoding fix using raw byte injection\n\n* fix: Final switch to pwsh for Windows environment detection and fixed resource paths\n\n* fix: Final partition for Unix cp paths and Windows ASCII environment encoding\n\n* fix: Final shell partition for Ruby tests to prevent Windows path corruption\n\n* fix: Robust Windows DLL discovery via System PATH and single INSTALL_PATH to resolve Error 126\n\n* fix: Targeted component discovery for Windows to resolve loader Error 126\n\n* fix: Final Windows dependency resolution via Ruby 3.5 sync and real-time PATH injection\n\n* fix: Skip setup-ruby on Windows and use bundled MetaCall Ruby 3.5 instead\n\n* fix: Define PYTHONHOME for bundled Windows runtime to resolve polyglot encodings error\n\n* fix: Robust resource copying and explicit PYTHONHOME for bundled Windows runtime\n\n* fix: Restore working Unix resource paths while preserving successful Windows polyglot logic\n\n* fix: Restore PythonHome detection for Windows and clean up Unix resource paths\n\n* ci: Implement robust cross-platform Ruby Gem release infrastructure\n\n* ci: Finalize robust cross-platform Ruby Gem release with explicit Windows PythonHome\n\n* fix: Robust Windows pathing and polyglot dependency resolution for Ruby Gem release\n\n* ci: Implement robust cross-platform Ruby Gem release infrastructure\n\n* ci: Simplify CI workflow to verify internal Ruby library discovery\n\n* feat: Enhance Ruby Port internal library discovery for cross-platform portability\n\n* feat: Implement internal library discovery and engine bootstrapping for Ruby Port\n\n* fix: Resolve Windows plugin dependency chain in Ruby Port internal discovery\n\n* fix: Bypass Ruby 3.x DLL security on Windows using SetDllDirectory\n\n* Update metacall.rb\n\n* Update metacall.rb\n\n* Update metacall.rb\n\n* Update metacall.rb\n\n* Update metacall.rb\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Vicente Eduardo Ferrer Garcia <7854099+viferga@users.noreply.github.com>",
